# Automatic text direction

Render user-facing strings with `AutoDir` from `@/components/AutoDir`. Do not drop raw copy into headings, paragraphs, addresses, or links.

- Persian / Arabic letters are RTL.
- Latin letters and ASCII digits (phones, emails, street addresses) isolate as LTR, even on `/fa`.
- If a string is only Latin/digits, set `dir="ltr"` on that block.
- If a string is only Persian, set `dir="rtl"` (or inherit).
- If a string mixes both, do **not** flip the whole block. Keep the page direction and isolate Latin runs with `<bdi>`. First-letter detection is not enough.
- Keep address blocks `block w-fit`, never `inline-block` next to Persian links.
- Form `input`, `textarea`, and `select` use `dir="auto"`.
